<article class="env-proposition" id="0D1C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0D1C">Proposition <span data-tag="0D1C">99.12.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $Z \to B$ and $X \to B$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$. Assume $X \to B$ is of finite presentation and separated and $Z \to B$ is of finite presentation, flat, and proper. Then $\mathit{Mor}_ B(Z, X)$ is an algebraic space locally of finite presentation over $B$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Immediate consequence of Lemma <a href="/tag/0D1B" data-tag="0D1B">99.12.2</a> and Proposition <a href="/tag/0D01" data-tag="0D01">99.9.4</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>